## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic demand paging, synchronization, and a tiny per-page state machine.

## Key Concepts
- Demand paging
- Per-page locking
- State machine: EMPTY, LOADING, READY
- Wait/wake and memory visibility

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: per-page fault path in a tiny OS
typedef enum { EMPTY, LOADING, READY } page_state_t;
typedef struct { page_state_t s; spinlock l; char *data; bool dirty; } page_t;
void handle_fault(page_t *p){
  acquire(&p->l);
  if (p->s==READY){ release(&p->l); return; }
  if (p->s==EMPTY){ p->s=LOADING; release(&p->l); read_disk_async(p); p->s=READY; wake_all(&p->wq); return; }
  while (p->s!=READY) wait(&p->wq, &p->l);
  release(&p->l);
}
```

